IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc1-s25-reports`

-- ccc1-tests-s25-reports.l4 -- tests for sections 25.2 to 25.4 of the Criminal Code (Canada). Expected values are written by hand from the text.
-- The regulative rules are run with #TRACE (a regulative outcome cannot be asserted on the stable binary); each is paired with a decision function that is asserted.
-- Clock of the traces: days for the rules without a WITHIN (nothing in the text gives a number); years from the commission for s 25.4(1), WITHIN 1.

§ `s 25.2  (the public officer files a report)`
#ASSERT `s 25.2 the public officer is required to file a written report with the appropriate senior official` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- acted under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) or (b): "shall ... file a written report"
#ASSERT `s 25.2 the public officer is required to file a written report with the appropriate senior official` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- any other act or omission: not covered
-- Expected by hand: the public officer files, so the duty is FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 25.2 the duty of the public officer to file a written report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 25.2 a public officer` DOES `s 25.2 file a written report with the appropriate senior official describing the act or omission` AT 3
-- Expected by hand: nothing is done and the clock runs, but the text sets no deadline, so the duty stays open (no breach is stated in the text without a time).
#TRACE `s 25.2 the duty of the public officer to file a written report` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§ `s 25.3  (the annual report)`
#ASSERT `s 25.3(1) the competent authority is required to publish or otherwise make available to the public an annual report for the previous year` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- every competent authority
#ASSERT `s 25.3(1) the competent authority is required to publish or otherwise make available to the public an annual report for the previous year` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- anyone else
#ASSERT `s 25.3(1) the annual report is required to include the item` `s 25.3(1)(a) the number of designations made under subsection 25.1(6) by the senior officials` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(1) the annual report is required to include the item` `s 25.3(1)(b) the number of authorizations made under paragraph 25.1(9)(a) by the senior officials` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(1) the annual report is required to include the item` `s 25.3(1)(c) the number of times that acts and omissions were committed in accordance with paragraph 25.1(9)(b) by the public officers` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(1) the annual report is required to include the item` `s 25.3(1)(d) the nature of the conduct being investigated when the designations referred to in paragraph (a) or the authorizations referred to in paragraph (b) were made or when the acts or omissions referred to in paragraph (c) were committed` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(1) the annual report is required to include the item` `s 25.3(1)(e) the nature of the acts or omissions committed under the designations referred to in paragraph (a), under the authorizations referred to in paragraph (b) and in the manner described in paragraph (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(1) the annual report is required to include the item` `s 25.3(1) another item` EQUALS NOTHING   -- "includes": the list is not closed
#ASSERT `s 25.3(2) the annual report is barred from containing the information` `s 25.3(2)(a) compromise or hinder an ongoing investigation of an offence under an Act of Parliament` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(2) the annual report is barred from containing the information` `s 25.3(2)(b) compromise the identity of a public officer acting in an undercover capacity, of a confidential informant or of a person acting covertly under the direction and control of a public officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(2) the annual report is barred from containing the information` `s 25.3(2)(c) endanger the life or safety of any person` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (c)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(2) the annual report is barred from containing the information` `s 25.3(2)(d) prejudice a legal proceeding` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (d)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(2) the annual report is barred from containing the information` `s 25.3(2)(e) otherwise be contrary to the public interest` EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (e)
#ASSERT `s 25.3(2) the annual report is barred from containing the information` `s 25.3(2) none of those` EQUALS NOTHING   -- none of the five effects: silent
-- Expected by hand: published, FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 25.3(1) the duty of the competent authority to publish an annual report` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 25.2 a competent authority` DOES `s 25.3 publish or otherwise make available to the public the annual report for the previous year` AT 100

§ `s 25.4(1)  (notification; no later than one year after the commission)`
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the senior official is required to notify the person in writing` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- an act under 25.1(9)(a) or (b), a report filed, property lost or seriously damaged
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the senior official is required to notify the person in writing` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not an act under 25.1(9)(a) or (b)
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the senior official is required to notify the person in writing` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no report filed under section 25.2
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the senior official is required to notify the person in writing` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- no property lost or seriously damaged
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the notification is no later than one year after the commission` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- on the day one year after the commission: "no later than one year after"
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the notification is no later than one year after the commission` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 14 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the day before
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the notification is no later than one year after the commission` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the day after
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the notification is no later than one year after the commission` (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- early notification
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the notification is no later than one year after the commission` (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- one year after 31 December 2025
#ASSERT `s 25.4(1) the notification is no later than one year after the commission` (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- the day after that
-- Expected by hand: notified within the year, FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 25.4(1) the duty of the senior official to notify in writing the person whose property was lost or seriously damaged` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 25.2 a senior official` DOES `s 25.4 notify in writing the person whose property was lost or seriously damaged` AT 0.5
-- Expected by hand: nothing is done in the year, so the duty is BREACHED.
#TRACE `s 25.4(1) the duty of the senior official to notify in writing the person whose property was lost or seriously damaged` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 1.5)

§ `s 25.4(2)  (authorization not to notify until the opinion)`
#ASSERT `s 25.4(2) the competent authority may authorize the senior official not to notify the person yet` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- the competent authority is not yet of the opinion that notification would not do any of the five things
#ASSERT `s 25.4(2) the competent authority may authorize the senior official not to notify the person yet` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- "until the competent authority is of the opinion that notification would not" do any of them: the authorization has run out
#ASSERT `s 25.4(2) the competent authority may authorize the senior official not to notify the person yet` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING   -- not the competent authority

§ `s 25.1(6), last sentence`
-- Expected by hand: notified, FULFILLED.
#TRACE `s 25.1(6) the duty of the senior official to notify the competent authority of the designation` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 25.2 a senior official` DOES `s 25.1(6) notify the competent authority of the designation` AT 1
